WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.646
With Transifex Native,

2
00:00:02.646 --> 00:00:06.268
strings stay in code, and
translations come from its delivery

3
00:00:06.268 --> 00:00:06.999
service.

4
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.357
Transifex does this well,

5
00:00:09.357 --> 00:00:11.133
with AI quality scores,

6
00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:13.965
partner vendors, and a
snippet for websites.

7
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.922
General Translation translates
your marked JSX with context,

8
00:00:18.922 --> 00:00:21.035
and bundles or serves the result.

9
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.669
Keep each sentence, with its links,

10
00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:26.155
inside a T component.

11
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.759
Then npx gt translate writes
the Japanese before the build.

12
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.833
With local translations,

13
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.633
the app renders bundled files,

14
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.234
with no runtime calls.

15
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.180
Your team now ships
Japanese with each release.
